Two parts of the operations request are not included, because the node's world cannot express them:

- **Log file:** the target is `wasm32-unknown-unknown` with no WASI filesystem, and the world has no file-writing capability.
- **Metadata fetch:** `metadata.internal.example` is outside the `HTTPClient<['feeds.example.com']>` allowlist, so the call would trap at the boundary. Sending the input's text to a host the node was not granted would also be an unapproved reach for authority.

If operations needs either, the graph should grant a log or metadata capability explicitly.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{heartbeat-report};

    import aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0;
    import aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0;
    import wasi:clocks/wall-clock@0.2.0;

    export run: func(feed-url: string) -> heartbeat-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::http_client;
use crate::aap::caps::notifier;
use crate::wasi::clocks::wall_clock;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(feed_url: String) -> HeartbeatReport {
        let seconds = wall_clock::now().seconds;

        let fetched = match http_client::fetch(&feed_url) {
            Ok(body) => body.chars().count() as u32,
            Err(_) => 0,
        };

        let message = format!("heartbeat at {} fetched {}", seconds, fetched);
        let mut notified = notifier::notify(&message);
        if !notified {
            notified = notifier::notify(&message);
        }

        HeartbeatReport {
            seconds,
            fetched,
            notified,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

